hi I'm Evan Carmichael and in today's  video I want to answer a question for  one of my readers to shock who asks how  can I start a business without a lot of  capital it's a great question and what I  want to remind you of is it's not so  much about how many resources you have  when you're starting out it's more about  how resourceful you are that will  determine how successful your company  will be as you grow so if you don't have  a lot of money to start at the business  that's okay what I applies entrepreneurs  to do is try to start a service-based  business instead of a product based  business that's number one product based  businesses are more expensive you have  inventory there might be a manufacturing  process you have to store your product  somewhere there's a lot more cost and if  you don't sell your product you've stuck  with all this extra inventory that you  can't get rid of we're a service-based  business the only cost really is your  time you may need some business cards  meaning the website to help you get  started but there's not a lot of other  costs that are associated with it it  also allows you to get really close to  your customers learn more about the  problems that they're facing and if you  then decide to launch a new product  afterwards you know the types of things  that they're really going to need so  think about a service-based business and  separate product based business to help  you get started the second thing I want  you to think about is you don't  necessarily have to start full time can  you do your business part time to get  you started so you have some momentum  going and you ensure that you have some  money coming in from another job that  may be on a part-time basis so it's  great if you can launch fallout into  your business but if you can't afford  that you can always turn the part-time  basis it's more important that you make  steps every day to build your business  even if it's on a part-time basis then  to advise tons of energy for three  months and doesn't take off and then you  shut down the business so if you have to  start hard time that's okay one thing i  want to remind you of and what I want  to think about is can you build your  business around the customer around the  pain customer so a lot of entrepreneurs  will start a business they think they  have the greatest idea in the world and  everyone is in by the product and then  they get out into the market and nobody  wants what they're selling the best way  to build a business is to find a  customer who has a problem and offer to  solve it if you can build your business  around paying customers you much more  likely to become successful and the last  thing I want to talk about is I would  strongly encourage you to follow your  passion a lot of entrepreneurs start a  business because they think you're going  to make a lot of money but they're not  really interested in whatever field  they're getting into it's almost always  a recipe for failure the most successful  entrepreneurs are the ones who follow  what they're really really excited about  passionate about it you can pour the  heart into and people see their  enthusiasm and they want to jump on  board and they want to hire you or they  want to buy your products or service so  really try to tap into what really makes  you tick what you're super excited about  and try to launch a business around that  passion so I hope that helped if you  enjoyed the video please leave a comment  below if you have any other questions  and also going to check out the comments  below and I also get the video it comes  up and we'll see you on the next episode  you
 

